   {
    "en": "MO"
   },
   {
    "en": "M₂O₃"
   },
   {
    "en": "MO₂"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 2,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "From M₃O₄ with 27.6% O: atomic mass of M = (72.4/27.6 × 64)/3 ≈ 56. In the second oxide, M : O = 70/56 : 30/16 = 1.25 : 1.875 = 2 : 3, so M₂O₃."
  },
